        <p><strong>Goal:</strong> A comprehensive analysis of how book pricing strategies relate to customer satisfaction across Fiction and Non-Fiction genres over a decade of Amazon bestseller data.</p>

        <h2 id="market-overview">1. Bestseller Market Overview (2009–2019)</h2>
        <div class="kpi-container">
            <div class="kpi">
                <div class="value">{total_books}</div>
                <div class="label">Total Bestsellers</div>
            </div>
            <div class="kpi">
                <div class="value">{genre_counts.get('Non Fiction', 0)} / {genre_counts.get('Fiction', 0)}</div>
                <div class="label">Non-Fiction / Fiction</div>
            </div>
            <div class="kpi">
                <div class="value">${avg_price:.2f}</div>
                <div class="label">Avg Price</div>
            </div>
            <div class="kpi">
                <div class="value">{avg_rating:.2f}</div>
                <div class="label">Avg Rating (0-5)</div>
            </div>
            <div class="kpi">
                <div class="value">{int(avg_reviews):,}</div>
                <div class="label">Avg Reviews</div>
